    "exact_reserve_text": "As a result of the adverse prior year loss development arising from the Russia/Ukraine losses and the Artisans sub class, the 2021 year of account is in a cumulative loss as at 31 December 2024. The casualty business group experienced deterioration to the prior year reserves as a result of construction defect claims in Florida. As a result of the settlements made and the uncertainty of outcomes, we have increased our loss reserves by a further GBP 128.9m gross and GBP 29.3m net of reinsurance recoveries for the western-leased aircraft in Russia. The ultimate reserved position for Florida based contractors moved from GBP 79.4m gross at the end of 2023, to a revised gross number of GBP 132.0m at the end of 2024. The 2022 year of account has closed with a profit of GBP 121.4m after all personal expenses but before members agents' fees, with a profit for the 2022 closed year of account at 36 months of GBP 133,817k.",
