    "standardized_narrative": "The syndicate experienced a net strengthening of prior year reserves by GBP 47.7 million in 2024. This was primarily driven by significant adverse development on the 2021 year of account due to increased loss reserves for western-leased aircraft in Russia (GBP 128.9 million gross strengthening) and deterioration in prior year reserves for Florida-based construction defect claims (GBP 52.6 million gross strengthening). Partially offsetting these strengthenings was a favorable development from the closure of the 2022 year of account, which reported a profit of GBP 133.8 million, indicating a release of reserves for that year.",
